From af4f143894cd6141207c99e8a65c7ddd6e2d4679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rakibul Islam <33988342+raykibul@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:36:46 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(desktop): make the new-session dialog a composer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Restores #154, reverted in #156 over the directory picker. The picker is
rebuilt in the commits that follow; this is the composer as it was.

The prompt is the dialog now — a single box that takes focus on open —
and the labelled selects become chips around it: the working directory
and the host across the top, provider, model and permissions along the
bottom. Each chip says its own value, so none of them needs a label.

The host chip shows even on a single host, because its dot is the
machine's connection state and "is it up" is worth answering before a
prompt is written rather than after the session fails to start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
